  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Tom, you're verified. I can refund the veggie burrito. It's $14.00, and the order has no promo discount.\n\nI can do either of these for the burrito:\n- **Refund of $14.00** to your Visa ending 4242.\n- **Account credit of $16.80** (the item price plus 20%) to use on a future order.\n\nWhich would you like?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Refund to the card please. The credit isn't much use to me, I'd rather have the actual money back."
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "issue_refund",
   "args": {
    "order_id": "K-8201",
    "amount": 14.0,
    "reason": "wrong_item",
    "item_ids": [
     "K-8201-1"
    ]
   },
   "result": {
    "refund_id": "RF-4000",
    "order_id": "K-8201",
    "amount": 14.0,
    "to": "Visa ending 4242",
    "arrives": "3-5 business days"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've refunded $14.00 for the veggie burrito to your Visa ending 4242. It should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok thanks. Before I go, I've had a few problems with orders over the past couple of months, not just this one. Why would that matter for a refund? Is my account getting flagged or something?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Your account isn't flagged, and nothing about your history held up today's refund.\n\nWe do look at how many refunds an account has had in the past 30 days. If an account reaches 3 or more support refunds in that window, we send further requests to a specialist for review instead of handling them directly. Refunds for items the restaurant marked unavailable don't count towards that.\n\nYou're below that threshold, so your requests are still handled normally. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, that makes sense. Thanks for the refund, I'll watch for it on my card. Nothing else from me."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Tom. Sorry again about the wrong burrito. Enjoy the rest of your evening!"
  }
